# Allow-list for scripts/audit_public.py: approved false positives only.
#
# Format, one entry per line:
#   <path-glob> <check-id>  # reason
#
# <path-glob> is an fnmatch glob against the repo-relative path; <check-id> is one of
# secret, denylist, transcript, host, path, artifact. The "# reason" is required: an
# entry without one is a usage error (exit 2). Matching findings are downgraded to info
# and shown as "allowed". Never put secret values or denylist terms in this file.
#
# Globs match the redacted path: a path containing a denylist term is shown as
# <denylist:N> and cannot be allowed by name (by design: such paths must not ship).
